  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG - Regional LWA-Asia: Asia-Pacific Regional Support for Elections and Political Transitions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Democracy, Conflict and Humanitarian Assistance (DCHA)):  .This mechanism will support improved election integrity and electoral justice in the Asia and Pacific region. With a qualified local organization delivering these services on a regional scale, USAID seeks to expand and diversify the base of organizations with which Missions can partner on electoral support programming and to increase the sustainability of development assistance in the elections and political transitions (EPT) arena. The award will provide USAID missions in Asia with a pre-competed mechanism for swift design and start-up of EPT programs. The award will strengthen elections and political processes in Asia through technical support and knowledge exchange among partner countries. During the program, national and local elections are anticipated in several countries in the region, and implementer Perludem will conduct targeted activities in selected countries to be determined depending on the political context and timing of these elections. Regional expertise will be shared through the country-specific activities and though regional workshops with electoral stakeholders. Perludem will develop and maintain an online database of election-related materials and regional EPT experts. To respond effectively to the rapidly evolving political environment in the region, the award will also include a Quick Response Fund to address emerging opportunities for engagement and programming. Fiscal year 2019 funds will support regional technical leadership, which may include work on regional standards for election administration and oversight. The award supports USAID priorities by providing electoral assistance to foster greater government accountability in partner countries. The emphasis on learning and information sharing will strengthen the effectiveness and sustainability of U.S. development investments, helping to ensure effectiveness and accountability to U.S. taxpayers, in line with the State-USAID</narrative>
  </description>
